  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nTemperatures are a bit on the toasty side with a ridge in place,\nbut not as high as a few models were suggesting. This has lead to\nsome potential instability at the surface, so any storm that\nbreaks the cap may be strong. The ridge is expected to slowly\nbreak down this weekend, so precipitation chances will return as\nwell as an upper trough moves in. The GFS and ECMWF ensembles \nsuggest there is high chance of seeing rainfall amounts over half \nan inch from Sunday through Tuesday north of the missouri river, \nand lower amounts south of the river. There is a decent chance of \nover an inch of accumulation north of Highway 2.\n\nAn airmass on the humid side is expected to move in from the east\non Sunday. Look for chances for showers and isolated strong thunderstorms\nin some areas on Sunday. A marginal risk of severe weather was\nissued for most of the area from SPC.\n\nAn upper ridge is expected to begin rebuilding on Tuesday night. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nMain deviations were a few adjustments to PoPs and winds through\n6 AM Sunday.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence of the red flag warning\nverifying in the southeast today since dewpoints are a bit higher\nthan expected there.\n\nThere is moderate confidence in rainfall amounts from Sunday\nthrough Tuesday.",
